    "blurb": "Typed AI decisions in BPMN",
    "overview": "Use Jev by TypeSafe AI in your Camunda processes. Make fast, typed AI decisions: pick the best option, find all matches, or ask yes/no, choice, and score questions over lists of any size.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Make fast, typed AI decisions in your processes",
    "splashDescription": "Make fast, typed AI decisions inside your Camunda processes with Jev, a decision model by TypeSafe AI. Instead of generating text, Jev returns typed answers with probabilities, so gateways and ad-hoc sub-processes can use the result directly with no parsing. The connector offers three operations. Choice picks the best option from a list of any size. Noul (yes/no scoring) finds every option that matches a request. Custom questions let you ask your own yes/no, choice, and score questions in one call. Large lists are handled automatically: Jev accepts up to 255 options per choice question, so the connector splits bigger lists into groups, runs rounds in parallel, and respects the token limit per call. Every response includes the process instance key, element ID, model version, token usage, and duration, and low-confidence decisions are flagged with needsReview for human review. For example, an ad-hoc sub-process contains 500 book tasks. When a user asks \"I need to lose weight,\" Jev selects the top 3 books, and only those 3 user tasks start. This is a community project and is not affiliated with TypeSafe AI.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/872567/overview/img2344031348208765548.png?62ba1261cc9521952ede1ccbd6b18231",
